#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# abs_arg_plot

#% text
# `abs_arg_plot(f, [x, a, b])` plots the modulus and the argument of f for x from a to b.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# It is `plot([abs(f), arg(f)], [x, a, b])`, and takes the options of `plot`.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% text
# A square:

#% cell
abs_arg_plot((x + im)^2, [x, -2, 2])
#% output
#= image("abs_arg_plot.files/abs_arg_plot-1.svgz")

#% subsection
# Scope

#% text
# The argument jumps where it wraps:

#% cell
abs_arg_plot(exp(2*im*x), [x, 0, 6])
#% output
#= image("abs_arg_plot.files/abs_arg_plot-2.svgz")

#% subsection
# Options

#% text
# With a legend:

#% cell
abs_arg_plot(1/(x + im), [x, -3, 3], plot_legends: ["modulus", "argument"])
#% output
#= image("abs_arg_plot.files/abs_arg_plot-3.svgz")

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `re_im_plot`, `plot`, `complex_plot`
